#!/bin/sh
# Forwards a Claude Code hook event to `mooring hook <Event>`. The hook JSON arrives on stdin and is
# left unread here: `exec` hands it to mooring. With no mooring found, or no event, it does nothing.
set -u

[ $# -ge 1 ] || exit 0

found=""
try() {
    if [ -z "$found" ] && [ -n "$1" ] && [ -x "$1" ] && [ ! -d "$1" ]; then found="$1"; fi
}

# 1. An explicit override.
try "${MOORING_BIN:-}"
# 2. The CLI link the app installs.
try "${HOME:-}/.local/bin/mooring"
# 3. mooring on PATH.
if [ -z "$found" ]; then
    try "$(command -v mooring 2>/dev/null || true)"
fi
# 4. The app that contains this script: .../Mooring.app/Contents/Resources/ClaudePlugin/mooring/scripts.
if [ -z "$found" ]; then
    here=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" 2>/dev/null && pwd -P) || here=""
    case "$here" in
        */Contents/Resources/ClaudePlugin/mooring/scripts)
            try "${here%/Resources/ClaudePlugin/mooring/scripts}/Helpers/mooring"
            ;;
    esac
fi
# 5. The installed app.
try "${MOORING_APPLICATIONS_DIR:-/Applications}/Mooring.app/Contents/Helpers/mooring"

[ -n "$found" ] || exit 0
exec "$found" hook "$1" 2>/dev/null
